    {
      "id": "yFYBxX7_fzjhxgtfGeG2Y",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -4097.499482900948,
      "y": 75.01021356715864,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 520,
      "strokeColor": "#c92a2a",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff5f5",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "Fn5pBOjSc18tAE0ZYYCDR"
      ],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1386874238,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 421798974,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBG",
      "frameId": null,
      "created": 1792310473371
    },
    {
      "id": "nQE_ufOAnuImcrbkCAcGS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4077.4994829009484,
      "y": 95.01021356715864,
      "width": 860,
      "height": 480,
      "text": "RESERVATION RULES\n\nRedis Lua script checks not-sold + no active competing hold,\nthen creates all selected hold keys atomically, or none.\nSame-event keys use {E1} for one Redis Cluster slot.\n\nA Redis success is provisional. PostgreSQL must atomically\nacquire the same seats before the client gets hold success.\nUse status / expiry conditions; versioning can guard updates.\nPostgreSQL records reservation_id and reserved_until.\nMirror the DB expiry as the remaining Redis TTL.\n\nDB conflict -> release only this reservation's Redis holds.\nUnknown DB outcome -> look up the reservation before release.\nNo payment -> Redis TTL expires; PostgreSQL treats its expired\nreservation as available when reading / acquiring seats.\nPayment starts only after the PostgreSQL hold succeeds.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "Fn5pBOjSc18tAE0ZYYCDR"
      ],
      "seed": 881370558,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 1271983230,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBH",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "created": 1792310473371,
      "originalText": "RESERVATION RULES\n\nRedis Lua script checks not-sold + no active competing hold,\nthen creates all selected hold keys atomically, or none.\nSame-event keys use {E1} for one Redis Cluster slot.\n\nA Redis success is provisional. PostgreSQL must atomically\nacquire the same seats before the client gets hold success.\nUse status / expiry conditions; versioning can guard updates.\nPostgreSQL records reservation_id and reserved_until.\nMirror the DB expiry as the remaining Redis TTL.\n\nDB conflict -> release only this reservation's Redis holds.\nUnknown DB outcome -> look up the reservation before release.\nNo payment -> Redis TTL expires; PostgreSQL treats its expired\nreservation as available when reading / acquiring seats.\nPayment starts only after the PostgreSQL hold succeeds.",
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TRk2GhUwXdTMiBKXrmQoh",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -3142.4994829009484,
      "y": 75.01021356715864,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 520,
      "strokeColor": "#6741d9",
      "backgroundColor": "#f3f0ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "yVhWgP7glq8aZlXhSPXkg"
      ],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1512652286,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 1446685886,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBI",
      "frameId": null,
      "created": 1792310473371
    },
    {
      "id": "dr4p8_vUUeFpnMn3NEl-r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3122.4994829009484,
      "y": 95.01021356715864,
      "width": 860,
      "height": 480,
      "text": "CONFIRMATION AND FAILURE RULES\n\nVerified provider success -> Booking Service -> PostgreSQL.\nIn one transaction, validate live reservation ownership,\nconfirm the booking and allocate ALL seats, or none.\nPostgreSQL prevents two confirmed owners of the same seat.\nReplayed callbacks return an already-committed booking.\n\nAfter commit: update Redis to BOOKED and remove stale holds.\nRedis failure does not invalidate the confirmed ticket.\nLog / monitor failures; reconciliation repairs Redis from DB.\nA PostgreSQL outbox is an optional reliable delivery mechanism.\n\nExpired / replaced hold or confirmed allocation conflict:\nno ticket; durably track a refund if payment was collected.\nStale Redis can cause failed attempts, not a second DB sale.\nDB commit unknown -> resolve by booking ID before refunding.\nNo Redis Stream is required in this PostgreSQL-first design.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "yVhWgP7glq8aZlXhSPXkg"
      ],
      "seed": 1754058302,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 637691134,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBJ",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "created": 1792310473371,
      "originalText": "CONFIRMATION AND FAILURE RULES\n\nVerified provider success -> Booking Service -> PostgreSQL.\nIn one transaction, validate live reservation ownership,\nconfirm the booking and allocate ALL seats, or none.\nPostgreSQL prevents two confirmed owners of the same seat.\nReplayed callbacks return an already-committed booking.\n\nAfter commit: update Redis to BOOKED and remove stale holds.\nRedis failure does not invalidate the confirmed ticket.\nLog / monitor failures; reconciliation repairs Redis from DB.\nA PostgreSQL outbox is an optional reliable delivery mechanism.\n\nExpired / replaced hold or confirmed allocation conflict:\nno ticket; durably track a refund if payment was collected.\nStale Redis can cause failed attempts, not a second DB sale.\nDB commit unknown -> resolve by booking ID before refunding.\nNo Redis Stream is required in this PostgreSQL-first design.",
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hkfWgIKjufsd0Pcg-TW7N",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -2187.4994829009484,
      "y": 75.01021356715864,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 520,
      "strokeColor": "#2b8a3e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ebfbee",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "nz_iIao5W3S8QA18XO8tx"
      ],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1016354430,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 1286149438,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBK",
      "frameId": null,
      "created": 1792310473371
    },
    {
      "id": "UqT5iL7dsfFvdEm8wfL7c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2167.4994829009484,
      "y": 95.01021356715864,
      "width": 860,
      "height": 480,
      "text": "REDIS OUTAGE, RECOVERY AND CAPACITY\n\nSeat-map reads fall back to PostgreSQL.\nSkip the Redis gate; run the SAME PostgreSQL hold operation.\nEvery successful hold still passes through PostgreSQL.\nMixed cached / bypass traffic cannot bypass DB ownership.\n\nUse PostgreSQL while Redis is unavailable or rebuilding.\nRepopulate Redis from DB-confirmed seats AND unexpired holds.\nDo not initialize a missing cache as all seats available.\nConditional refreshes must not overwrite a newer reservation.\n\nRedis absorbs read traffic and competing hold attempts.\nPostgreSQL receives all successful holds + payment work.\nUse tighter admission limits during an outage if necessary.\nAvailability / throughput can degrade; ownership must not.\n\nEvent creation and booking-window initialization are deferred.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "groupIds": [
        "nz_iIao5W3S8QA18XO8tx"
      ],
      "seed": 1862325950,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 59751806,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792310480064,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "bBL",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "created": 1792310473371,
      "originalText": "REDIS OUTAGE, RECOVERY AND CAPACITY\n\nSeat-map reads fall back to PostgreSQL.\nSkip the Redis gate; run the SAME PostgreSQL hold operation.\nEvery successful hold still passes through PostgreSQL.\nMixed cached / bypass traffic cannot bypass DB ownership.\n\nUse PostgreSQL while Redis is unavailable or rebuilding.\nRepopulate Redis from DB-confirmed seats AND unexpired holds.\nDo not initialize a missing cache as all seats available.\nConditional refreshes must not overwrite a newer reservation.\n\nRedis absorbs read traffic and competing hold attempts.\nPostgreSQL receives all successful holds + payment work.\nUse tighter admission limits during an outage if necessary.\nAvailability / throughput can degrade; ownership must not.\n\nEvent creation and booking-window initialization are deferred.",
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    }
  ],
